WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.600
Asyncio.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:07.733
The core skill for LLM engineering, because LLM systems spend nearly all their time waiting.

3
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:12.467
Asyncio is single-threaded, cooperative concurrency.

4
00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:15.821
A function defined with async def is a coroutine.

5
00:00:15.821 --> 00:00:19.000
It runs until it awaits something that isn't ready.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.367
Then it hands control to the event loop.

7
00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:23.833
Here's the loop at work.

8
00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.800
It runs a task until that task hits an await.

9
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.767
The task is parked while its network call is out.

10
00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.567
Meanwhile the loop runs the next ready task.

11
00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:36.833
When the response lands, the parked task resumes right after its await.

12
00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.933
Three tools cover most of the work.

13
00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:43.467
Gather fans out many awaits and collects every result.

14
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:48.633
A semaphore caps how many run at once, so five hundred calls don't melt a rate limit.

15
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:50.500
And wait for adds a timeout.

16
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.200
Here's the pattern in code.

17
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.700
The semaphore allows only five requests out at a time.

18
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.900
The await parks the task while the response travels.

19
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.064
Gather launches a task per day.

20
00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:05.733
Twenty calls finish in about four round trips, on one thread.

21
00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.903
Never call blocking code inside a coroutine.

22
00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:12.400
One blocking call freezes every task.

23
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.433
Use the async versions, and push heavy computing to an executor.

24
00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:18.633
Why it matters.

25
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:22.633
The research agent's question needs three different APIs.

26
00:01:22.933 --> 00:01:26.233
One by one, you wait for all three latencies added up.

27
00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:28.800
With gather, you wait only for the slowest.

28
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.760
Let's recap.

29
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.800
Await means: park me, loop, go run someone else.

30
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.533
Gather fans out and a semaphore limits.

31
00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:39.061
And never block inside a coroutine.

32
00:01:39.061 --> 00:01:40.333
Next up: type hints.
